{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-12T14:24:52.111Z","author":"pi-glm-tooling","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"f97248eb555a999d6e67e9b1","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-lint-1c6j"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Declare the schema capability so packed command flags activate"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Packed-consumer acceptance (pm package install of the tarball) fails activation: registerCommand flags requires capability 'schema' in extension manifest capabilities. manifest.json currently declares capabilities [commands] only; registerLintCommand registers repeatable flags, so the manifest must also declare schema (capabilities: commands, schema). Verified against the packed tarball install path."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Task"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":[]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-10-12T14:24:52.111Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-12T14:24:52.111Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"pi-glm-tooling"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-lint-cli"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"503afbb9080ad82dad96e30fc29406497afe79d7b77fe4e7763e4b8c0f12455b","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"e564f75abb06637d4000965067cd12180649e9671c5ef8040c72a66ee380743f"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-12T14:28:09.555Z","author":"pi-glm-tooling","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"f97248eb555a999d6e67e9b1","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-12T14:28:09.555Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-10-12T14:28:09.555Z","author":"pi-glm-tooling","text":"Packed-tarball verification found two more real-host contract gaps in the command registration, beyond the schema capability already described: (1) the real host derives allowed option keys from FlagDefinition.long by stripping exactly two leading dashes, so long: '--disable <value>' registers the key 'disable <value>' and every flag use fails with Unknown option '--disable' while the SDK testing harness accepts it; fix by declaring long without the value placeholder (for example long: '--disable', value_name: 'value'), and note FlagDefinition exposes list rather than repeatable for repeatable string flags (see pm-jev flags: long '--full', value_type, value_name). (2) the host readHandlerResultExitCode contract requires that a command result not carry an exit_code own property of 0: exit_code must be 1..255 and present only on failure, so runLintCommand must omit exit_code when the verdict passes (return the verdict without the exit_code key on success, keep exit_code: 1 when findings meet fail_on). The manifest.json schema capability is required for any registerCommand with flags: pm package install refused activation with hint 'registerCommand flags requires capability schema in extension manifest capabilities' until capabilities became [commands, schema]; that one-line manifest.json change is applied in the package worktree for verification and needs to be committed with the CLI work."}]}],"before_hash":"503afbb9080ad82dad96e30fc29406497afe79d7b77fe4e7763e4b8c0f12455b","after_hash":"8bd9c7c29d4ba0902bd0baf2d2d8194ac44ef5412082d8c0699c66038a4ba3ed","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"b4ea12d889f46abb7aead6c3c3306e561720b492846ed01d0adeb45fa1354487"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-12T14:36:08.030Z","author":"codex-sol","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"eea1efbfed9603302cd01e6d","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-12T14:36:08.030Z","author":"codex-sol","text":"Host adapter now resolves the recorded flag registration and successful exit-control gaps. Packed npm/npx and native Bun/bunx acceptance passes 1/1 with repeated disable flags, TOON JSON and complete corpus counts. SDK testing dispatch remains covered alongside actual CLI acceptance."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-12T14:36:08.030Z"}],"before_hash":"8bd9c7c29d4ba0902bd0baf2d2d8194ac44ef5412082d8c0699c66038a4ba3ed","after_hash":"fe5b5de03adfaa818732f1a212a6ca0430bd401507eb6868bbfe31f0c6a4d823","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"13b5448ed9491b5d55852fd4ecd0710b574bd39a9c4a261b3bd93bd51aa1579e"}
